{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-skew-poisson-integration","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:skew-poisson-integration","kind":"proposition","title":"Integration of skewed-Poisson structures","proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-skew-poisson-integration"],"cites":["references/leitner2006"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.FormalGroups.integrationMk_commutator","text":"skew-poisson-integration.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:skew-poisson-integration\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> be a field and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{H_i, H\\}</code> be a commutative geometric formal group over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> (Leitner, Definition 3.1). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> be the splay of the distribution algebras <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_i = \\mathrm{Dist}(H_i)</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code> be a Poisson structure on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> that is both strongly filtered and strongly multiplicative (Definition 1.11: the comultiplication of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> induced from the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_i</code> satisfies the strong-multiplicativity identity with respect to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J \\subset T</code> be the ideal generated by the elements <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">fg - gf - \\pi(f, g)</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f, g \\in T</code>, and put</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">U \\;=\\; T / J.</code></pre>\n<p>Then (Leitner, Theorem 3.7) <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code> is the distribution algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Dist}(G)</code> of a formal group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{H_i, G\\}</code> is a geometric formal group.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/skew-poisson-integration.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"5.8.2","page":"b/prop-skew-poisson-integration","qa":{"counts":{"pass":96,"fail":0,"warn":4,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":118},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.PBWFormalGroup.formalGroup_of_splay","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/PBWFormalGroup.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
